  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "An exploded view of a generic examination room after the magnifier located the sections: the two label cards (\"Factual discrepancy\" ● and \"Legal question raised\" ◆ — neutral labels supplied by the party, glyph and placeholder bars only) leave the board through the top wall to a band above the room, card A to one side and card B, mirrored, to the other, and the numbered placeholder sections lift off the table to an enlarged row between them; the party stays at the table with the magnifier laid back. Each piece is labelled on the plan. Only the supplied relationships are drawn, with their kind captioned on the plan (the party supplies each label; each label is attached to its located section, as supplied); a relationship and its mirror are drawn together. A tracer follows the supplied traversal and a second one its mirror, at the same time; the element reached enlarges, the focus most. Both cards get the same neutral frame. Illustrative; nothing is evaluated, no section is said to be wrong, neither label is preferred and no outcome is drawn.",
